From a9d01e0e73605729b54a170965c2dfbf9d58c03e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 02:18:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] perf(gouraud asm): delete the per-triangle setup, not the
 fill

Census (300 frames, moving lumbridge): 13,359 triangles reach the
trapezoid walks per frame and pay ~275 instructions of fixed setup
each -- ~49% of the kernel's instruction stream -- for 31 pixels.

- SEGMENT takes its real slots as arguments; the six generic slots,
  V_HSL and V_SAREA are gone and the edges/colour stay in registers
  across the segment boundary.  -38 instr/triangle.
- The redundant ish16 equality test leaves both row loops, and the
  1..3-px tail indexes an 8-byte table instead of xor/cmp/setge.
- NOHCLIP and the unclamped row loop are deleted; the general clamped
  loop runs every row, which cannot move a pixel.

1123 -> 603 static instructions, 4160 -> 2336 bytes.
test-gouraud-tri-asm: PASS, 200000 triangles, every pixel identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
